From a878358584c0bf79db14a946950c1e0fef9ff402 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: FreeholdOS Build <build@freeholdos.local>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 02:04:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: refuse location-gated access to an app with a persona

Scan results, the scanner, suggestions, Aware, ranging and Wi-Fi Direct all pass WifiPermissionsUtil. An app with a persona now fails the location checks there (enforceLocationPermission, the fine and coarse variants, both scan-result checks, the nearby-devices check when it requires location, and Wi-Fi Direct), so none of those paths shows it the real surroundings.
---
 .claude/work/compartments-profiles.md         |  1 +
 .../server/wifi/util/WifiPermissionsUtil.java | 24 +++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 25 insertions(+)
 create mode 100644 .claude/work/compartments-profiles.md

diff --git a/.claude/work/compartments-profiles.md b/.claude/work/compartments-profiles.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..1650364
--- /dev/null
+++ b/.claude/work/compartments-profiles.md
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+2026-10-31T02:02 [DECISION] 2026-10-31 P8 Wi-Fi: persona guard (PersonaReader.placeOf(uid)!=0 -> SecurityException / false) added centrally in WifiPermissionsUtil enforceLocationPermission, enforceFine/CoarseLocationPermission, enforceCanAccessScanResults, enforceCanAccessScanResultsForWifiScanner, enforceNearbyDevicesPermission(checkForLocation only), checkCanAccessWifiDirect; repo .worktrees/rest-fixes/wifi; rejected: per-feature hooks in Aware/RTT/P2P (all route through these). Next: bluetooth same way, then format-patch + git am.
diff --git a/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/util/WifiPermissionsUtil.java b/service/java/com/android/server/wifi/util/WifiPermissionsUtil.java
